senses.gloss:
ādeśanā,
(1) (= Pali ādesanā-, cpd. with pāṭihāriya), reading of the mind: Bbh 〔264.21〕 sa ṛddhyā cittādeśanayā … (sattvān vinayati); usually in cpd. ādeśanā-prātihārya, trick or marvelous ability of mind-reading, reading other peopleʼs thoughts, see s.v. prātihārya;
(2) in dakṣiṇādeśanā (once ˚na), assignment of profit of good deeds, see that cpd.
